# KLAIM 2025 revision 2 -- 3D case list (one job per line, 64 cores each). Lines starting with # are ignored.
# columns: name  wsteg  material  gc  sig_y  hard  embedding  crack_factor  [geometry: porous (default) | strip | solid]  [newton_min_iters or -]  [nl: NL_FRACTURE, default 5, or -]  [nholes: default 6 or -]  [h_band: fixed band element size or -]  [cores: default 64]
#   solid = the w_s = 1 box without pores and with the yield stress everywhere (one homogeneous vM material) -> J_c^num of the 3D discretization
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S1_3D: paper sweep (vM), eta = 1e-5, beta = 0.2
S1_3D_vM_ws0.25    0.25  vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
S1_3D_vM_ws0.375   0.375 vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
S1_3D_vM_ws0.5     0.5   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
S1_3D_vM_ws0.75    0.75  vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
S1_3D_vM_ws1.0     1.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
S1_3D_vM_ws2.0     2.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
S1_3D_vM_ws3.0     3.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
S1_3D_vM_ws4.0     4.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S3_3D: cubic embedding (R1 major point 4), reference w_s
S3_3D_cubic_vM_ws1.0   1.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 cubic 1.0
S3_3D_cubic_vM_ws0.375 0.375 vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 cubic 1.0
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S2_3D: homogeneous reference (no pores), 2026-10-17
S2_3D_solid_vM     1.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 solid
# 2026-10-19: the 3D fracture mesh scales with the domain (element size in the crack band = L_domain/NL/n_ref = 0.08 w_cell,
# i.e. 0.10 L at w_s = 0.25 ... 0.40 L at w_s = 4.0, eps = 0.1 L) -> J_c^num,3D depends on w_s; one solid reference per w_s mesh
S2_3D_solid_vM_ws0.25   0.25  vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 solid
S2_3D_solid_vM_ws0.375  0.375 vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 solid
S2_3D_solid_vM_ws0.5    0.5   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 solid
S2_3D_solid_vM_ws0.75   0.75  vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 solid
S2_3D_solid_vM_ws2.0    2.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 solid
S2_3D_solid_vM_ws3.0    3.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 solid
S2_3D_solid_vM_ws4.0    4.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 solid
# 2026-10-19 mesh convergence at the coarse end (w_s = 4: NL = 5 -> element size 0.40 L = 4 eps in the crack band)
#S2_3D_solid_vM_ws4.0_nl10  4.0 vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 solid  - 10
# porous convergence series at w_s = 4 with a 3-pore specimen (evaluation window = ligament before pore 3 is still inside;
# band element size = L/NL/20 with L = (nholes + 2) w_cell = 25): NL 3 / 4 / 5 -> 4.2 / 3.1 / 2.5 eps. NL 8 on the 6-pore specimen
# (4x the elements of S1_3D_vM_ws4.0) would not finish before the deadline.
#S8_3D_vM_ws4.0_nh3_nl3     4.0 vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 porous 5 3 3
#S8_3D_vM_ws4.0_nh3_nl4     4.0 vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 porous 5 4 3
#S8_3D_vM_ws4.0_nh3_nl5     4.0 vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 porous 5 5 3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S7_3D: same cases with NEWTON_MIN_ITERS = 5 (2026-10-19)
# the S1_3D runs below sit at 4 Newton iterations per step, so dt never grows after a cut-back (frozen at 1e-5 .. 8e-5);
# columns + geometry + newton_min_iters
S7_3D_vM_ws0.5_mi5         0.5   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 porous 5
S7_3D_vM_ws0.75_mi5        0.75  vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 porous 5
S7_3D_vM_ws1.0_mi5         1.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 porous 5
S7_3D_cubic_vM_ws0.375_mi5 0.375 vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 cubic     1.0 porous 5
S7_3D_vM_ws2.0_mi5         2.0   vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 porous 5
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S6_3D (optional, comment in if the queue allows): elastic reference sets in 3D
#S6_3D_EqJc_ws1.0    1.0   elastic 1.0    1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
#S6_3D_EqSig_ws1.0   1.0   elastic 0.5523 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S1F/S2F/S9F (2026-10-19): fixed element size along the crack path
# mesh_fracture_adaptive.py --h_band: target h in |y| < 0.35 L, 2h in |y| < 0.65 L (whole central pore row), independent of
# the domain length -> the same resolution for every w_s (measured median edge in the band: 1.49 eps for h = 0.1, 1.03 eps for
# h = 0.07; the S1_3D meshes above have 1.7 / 2.4 / 3.6 / 6.4 eps at w_s = 0.5 / 1 / 2 / 4). 4 pores along x (the 3D
# evaluation uses the ligament before pore 2), NEWTON_MIN_ITERS = 5. Tets: 85k / 103k / 141k / 185k / 416k (w_s 0.375-2.0),
# 505k for h = 0.07 at w_s = 1. One solid reference per h is enough (band size independent of w_s); ws2.0 checks that.
# 2026-10-20: 128 cores on 2 nodes failed at the first parallel XDMF/HDF5 write ("Failed to create HDF5 file", both jobs,
# 15:47 on 19.10) -> 96 cores on ONE node (all nodes have >= 96 cores); multi-node runs are avoided.
# name                        wsteg material gc  sig_y hard      embedding crack geometry nmi nl nholes h_band cores
S1F_3D_vM_ws0.375             0.375 vonmises 1.0 1.0 0.2222222 isotropic 1.0 porous   5   -  4      0.1    64
